# Build context hygiene.
#
# The Dockerfile reads exactly three things: Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock and src/.
# Without this file the whole checkout is streamed to the build daemon on every
# build — locally that means the 2.6 GB cargo `target/` directory and the git
# history, and on a runner it means every build of the e2e/compat images pays for
# material it never looks at. The generated e2e key material
# (e2e-tests/data/**, private RSA + TLS keys) must never enter a build context
# either.

.git
.gitignore
target
e2e-tests
charts
deploy
docs
k8s
scripts
tests
*/*.md
*.md
LICENSE
.dockerignore
